Z||000000||mad dog||06-17-2000||11:02 AM||||More questions on something I posted and got responses on back on 5/16.  86 Fiero SE has a rough ride.  The right rear tire had a wear pattern on inside and actually caused a piece of the tire to split off!  When driving the car (before this and now with 2 new rear tires), it feels as if it is swaying and/or gently rocking.  It seems the motion is "out of synch" with each side--going slightly forward and backward on each side of the car at different times.  My next step is to get the rotors checked.  It also seems to drift when on the highway--almost like a slight kick out of the rear end--and this is when going straight.  I'd appreciate any additional suggestions.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phaeton||06-17-2000||01:18 PM||||A technician aligning my Fiero rears attached the laser alignment plate crooked and the Fiero acted similar. It might be worth having the alignment checked again, errors creep in.||||reg||12
Z||000002||lowCG||06-17-2000||02:28 PM||||Sounds like the toe-in is way off,is it twitchy,wanting to oversteer easily?||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||06-17-2000||03:42 PM||||when were the rear struts replaced last?||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||06-17-2000||11:06 PM||||Sounds like an alignment problem to me, probably the rear toe setting. It causes the tires to wear very fast and they become feathered.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mad dog||06-18-2000||12:54 PM||||Thanks for the input. Shocks & struts were replaced approx. 33,000 miles ago and car was aligned at about same time.  I believe the car is slightly twitchy--or a better way of saying it for my car is that it feels the same as when you reach a stretch of road that has "uneven pavement" and it causes the car to feel like it hit an uneven groove.  Also the Fiero has a lot going on in the backend when just riding in a straight line at 45-60 miles an hour.  It doesnt feel good and tight like it should.  Lastly, do you  have any recommendation on quality repair shops in the Jupiter/Stuart/West Palm Beach Florida area?  My current mechanic is fairly good--but this might be too much for him to handle.  Let me know asap.  Thanks again!||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GT||06-18-2000||11:01 PM||||Ogre(I think) mentioned in another post that cradle bushings and motor mounts could play a part in the uneasy twitchy feeling.  The wear pattern on your car is probably from the toe being way off.  Mine was when I had it aligned and my tires were worn badly on the inner halves.||||reg||1
Z||000007||StuGood||06-19-2000||02:07 PM||||You know a guy's serious when he's willing to drive all the way to Jupiter to get his Fiero aligned!<P>Be sure to make a pit stop at Mars, unless you have the larger 1987-88 tank  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000008||lowCG||06-19-2000||06:44 PM||||Also check the control arm bushings back there,before having that alignment re-done,a Fiero with decent shocks/tires shouldn't feel busy until twice that speed.||||reg||1
